# Planted-bug (mutation) tests, DESIGN.md §7.4. Everything below the "command:" line is the complete
# output of that command (stdout; then the wall time from /usr/bin/time -p). The notes in this header
# were written after the run.
#
# Result: the unmodified RTL PASSES on both vector sets; all 9 planted bugs FAIL on the corner set.
#
# Notes:
# - Why two vector sets. On the first 300 recorded decisions, 3 mutants PASS: 02 (omega wraps),
#   03 (tie-break with <=) and 05 (h clamps at 255). They are not equivalent designs. They are
#   equivalent ON THAT DATA: those 300 decisions never saturate omega, never clamp an h and never
#   have a tied best cost (coverage line below), and the mutated logic only differs from the
#   correct logic in exactly those cases. The stimulus never asked the question. The corner set
#   (all 71 decisions out of 4,000 that hit one of those cases, plus the earliest others) catches
#   all three, and the counts match the corner cases exactly: 02 fails in the 20 omega-saturating
#   decisions, 05 in the 32 h-clamping ones, 03 in the 27 tied ones (only best_idx; the costs and
#   states are right), 01 in the 48 decisions where theta wraps.
# - 06 (no 21/32 weight) and 09 (omega' written back one clock late, so its cost squares the old
#   omega) leave every final state right: 0 state failures. Only the cost check (and the best
#   check, through best_cost) sees them. That is why the testbench compares costs and states
#   separately.
# - 07 (one imagined step short) passes the best check in 2 of the first 300 decisions. One-off
#   check with model/golden.py's int_rollout (14 vs 15 steps, decisions 0..299): in decisions 258
#   and 259 the best candidate's 15th step costs 0 (theta' = 0, |omega'| <= 1, |u| <= 45: the
#   pendulum is balanced), so best_idx and best_cost come out the same. Its costs and states still
#   fail in all 300. 07 also runs 83 fewer clocks per decision (1198, not 1281), but the clock
#   check compares the engine's cycles output with the testbench's count of the same clocks, so
#   that check cannot see it.
# - Every mutant compiled with iverilog -g2005 -Wall without a warning (no compiler output below).
# - The harness itself was checked in a scratch copy of the repo (not committed): a sed script that
#   matches nothing is reported "not applied", a copy that does not compile "compile error" (both
#   make the run fail, they are never counted as caught), and an FSM that never finishes "FAIL
#   watchdog".
#
################################################################
# command: PYTHON=<venv python> bash mutants/run_mutants.sh   (what "make mutants" runs, see mutants/run_mutants.sh)
# Planted-bug tests (DESIGN.md §7.4): bash mutants/run_mutants.sh
# started 2026-10-12 20:31:32, Icarus Verilog version 13.0 (stable) (v13_0)
# rtl/ and tb/ from commit 43a549e (0 uncommitted changes), N = 300 decisions per run, LANES = 32

Vector sets (corner cases replayed through the golden model):
  recorded vectors (sim/, H = 15), all 4000 decisions: h clamped at 127 in 32 (133 times), theta wraps in 272 (8052 times), omega saturates in 20 (228 times), tied best cost in 27
  first 300 (sim/ as recorded): 300 decisions: h clamped at 127 in 0 (0 times), theta wraps in 9 (288 times), omega saturates in 0 (0 times), tied best cost in 0
  corner 300 (sim/mutants/vec/): 300 decisions: h clamped at 127 in 32 (133 times), theta wraps in 48 (1327 times), omega saturates in 20 (228 times), tied best cost in 27
    = all 71 decisions with an h clamp, an omega saturation or a tie, plus the first 229 others (decisions 0..3955)

Each result column: PASS or FAIL, then how many of the 300 decisions failed each
testbench check: costs / final states / best (best_idx or best_cost wrong).
A mutant must FAIL.

mutant               | what it models                                                     | first 300          | corner 300        
-------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------ | ------------------
00_original          | nothing planted: the RTL as committed                              | PASS 0/0/0         | PASS 0/0/0        
01_theta_saturates   | theta saturates at +-127 instead of wrapping                       | FAIL 9/9/9         | FAIL 48/48/38     
02_omega_wraps       | omega wraps (keeps the low 8 bits) instead of saturating           | PASS 0/0/0         | FAIL 20/20/4      
03_argmin_last_tie   | argmin compares with <=, so a tie picks the LAST index             | PASS 0/0/0         | FAIL 0/0/27       
04_logical_shift     | logical >> instead of arithmetic >>> in requantization             | FAIL 300/300/300   | FAIL 300/300/300  
05_h_clamp_255       | hidden values clamp at 255 instead of 127                          | PASS 0/0/0         | FAIL 32/32/7      
06_no_omega_weight   | omega cost term is omega'^2, the 21/32 weight dropped              | FAIL 300/0/300     | FAIL 300/0/300    
07_one_step_short    | off-by-one in the step loop: imagines H-1 steps, not H             | FAIL 300/300/298   | FAIL 300/300/300  
08_l2_no_bias        | layer-2 dot products never restart from the bias                   | FAIL 300/300/300   | FAIL 300/300/300  
09_omega_wb_late     | omega' written back one clock late: its cost uses the OLD omega    | FAIL 300/0/269     | FAIL 300/0/273    

first 300 decisions:  6 of 9 mutants caught
corner 300 decisions: 9 of 9 mutants caught
wall time: 294 s (4 simulations at a time)
